From 6a9440fdb40b6e6c555b461f3b3c7c9bdf2e46c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 18:14:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fix logo overlap, admin delete confirmation, tracking gap,
 lint

Five small fixes on top of the command center.

1. CrankcaseBadge: the wordmark could run straight into the GARAGE chip.
   The text had no width constraint, so its layout depended entirely on
   Big Shoulders Display actually loading -- when that font is slow,
   blocked, or unavailable the far wider fallback overlapped the chip.
   Pinned both text elements with textLength + lengthAdjust so the mark is
   now font-independent, and added condensed fallbacks to --font-display so
   a substitute needs less squeezing. Verified with the font blocked
   entirely: CRANKCASE ends at x=252, the chip starts at x=262.

2. /admin/users ignored the ?ok= and ?error= params that the account-delete
   handler redirects back with, so a successful deletion looked like nothing
   had happened. It now renders them.

3. Custom vehicles had no view tracking. Those are exactly the vehicles in
   the admin demand backlog, so they were the most useful views to capture
   and the only ones being missed.

4. Removed a redundant synchronous setState inside an effect in
   CustomVehicleClient (initial state was already "loading") and an unused
   router in ResetPasswordForm. Documented why layout.tsx loads its font
   with a plain <link> instead of next/font/google -- that switch fails the
   BUILD for this font, and the warning was inviting someone to "fix" it.

5. Deleted Header-1.tsx, PrintServiceHistory-1.tsx and
   PrintVehicleSpecSheet-1.tsx -- stray duplicates, referenced nowhere.

One lint error remains, in AddVehicleClient. It is pre-existing and clearing
it properly means restructuring a component that shipped hours ago; not worth
the regression risk for a lint-only issue.

